 "text": "Geographic Information Systems - Otter Tail County, MN\nSkip to content\nEnglish Español Afsoomaali Hmong العربية Tiếng Việt Bosanski Norsk bokmål Svenska Deutsch Français\nEnglish\nMenu\nEvent Calendar\nContact\nPay\nApply or Register\nServices\nAssistance & Support\nBusiness & Workforce Development\nElections and Voting\nEnvironment & Natural Resources\nLicenses, Permits, Records & Inspections\nParks & Recreation\nProperty & Home\nPublic Safety & Law\nRecycling & Waste Disposal\nRoads & Transportation\nVisitors\nGovernment\nAbout Otter Tail County\nOur Long-Range Strategic Plan\nCities\nTownships\nLocations\nDepartments\nBoards & Commissions\nServe Your County\nPolicies & Ordinances (opens in new tab)\nProjects\nRequests for Data or Public Records\nSafety Data Sheets (opens in new tab)\nEmployment\nDepartments\nGeographic Information Systems\nThe GIS department provides essential services to Ottertail County:\nE911 Address System – Manage and maintain the county’s E911 address system for emergency services.\nMaps – Expand and maintain all interactive maps .\nGIS Database Development – Plan, develop, and implement GIS spatial and attribute databases that support decision-making.\nData Analysis – Use programs created to manipulate and analyze spatial data for planning and problem solving.\nTechnical Support – Serve as a technical resource for other county departments.\nVisit the Maps and Data hub\nServices\nMaps & Data\nView all County Services related to this department\nResources\nMinnesota GIS/LIS Consortium (opens in new tab) — Provides programs and activities to support professionals and students.\nPine 2 Prairie GIS User Group (opens in new tab) — Information on regional GIS events, news, and activities for everyone.\nMinnesota Geospatial Commons (opens in new tab) — A place for professionals and citizens who use GIS data to collaborate.\nContact\nFor general inquiries, please contact:\n218-998-8310 (opens in new tab)\ngis@ottertailcounty.gov (opens 